---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies on ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: none set by the site`} description="The sales tax and property tax calculators set no cookie, and nor does the site. Stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode, content masked." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>The sales tax, reverse sales tax and property tax calculators never need a cookie, and the site shows no advertising.</p>
    <h2>No cookies</h2><p>No page of the site sets a cookie, and the calculators store nothing on your device: prices, local rates and home values stay in the open page and disappear when you close it. That is why there is no cookie banner: there is nothing to accept.</p>
    <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2><p>To catch broken pages, script errors, slow loading and dead buttons, the site loads Microsoft Clarity in its cookie-free mode. Clarity then sets no cookie (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), gives every page view its own one-off identifier and does not link visits together. Page content and anything you type are masked before data is sent.</p>
    <h2>Blocking it</h2><p>Blocking the clarity.ms domain, or using a content blocker, stops this monitoring too; the calculators work just the same.</p>
    <p>More in the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
